OL,3,GNEWSAExhibition explores 80 years of
OL,4,AAfrican-Caribbean history
OL,5,
OL,6,FFrom Windrush stories to community
OL,7,Fcampaigns and a thriving reggae scene -
OL,8,Fa new exhibition is exploring the
OL,9,Fpeople and organisations that have
OL,10,Fhelped shape Wolverhampton over the
OL,11,Fpast 80 years.
OL,13,FThe free display, at Wolverhampton City
OL,14,FArchives, has opened for Black History
OL,15,FMonth and traces African-Caribbean
OL,16,Fhistory in the city.
OL,18,FThrough photographs, publications, oral
OL,19,Fhistories and community projects, it
OL,20,Fshines a light on the people and
OL,21,Forganisations behind decades of change
OL,22,Fin the city.
